+A follow-up simulation tested the known NB2 generating scale at nominal
+level 0.90 on 32 datasets per scenario. All 9,504 paired bootstrap refits
+completed with 99 draws per dataset. In the interior scenario, both the
+bootstrap and chi-squared likelihood-ratio tests included the generating
+scale in 24 of 32 datasets. They agreed on every decision. The exact 95%
+binomial interval for inclusion was 0.566 to 0.885.
+
+In the weak-effect scenario, the bootstrap included 27 of 32 generating
+scales and the chi-squared test included 26. One dataset was included only
+by the bootstrap. Near the upper bound under the Poisson limit, the
+bootstrap included 27 of 32 and the chi-squared test included 29. Two
+datasets were included only by the chi-squared test. The bootstrap
+Monte Carlo limits crossed the rejection cutoff in four interior, five
+weak-effect, and five near-bound datasets. These are paired comparisons
+of pointwise inclusion. Coverage of the returned finite-grid sets also
+depends on the grid and its accepted components.
 
